Darwin variadic cursors and named stack arguments — 2026-10-16

Two failures from the unchanged return-signing runtime are repaired:
1. Both interpreters treated Darwin's eight-byte list as a 32-byte list.
   Memory start/access/copy/overlap now use the selected target layout.
   C-HIR va_copy does too. The EvoIR program entry also receives that target;
   it previously rebuilt a Linux layout before init/main/fini execution.
2. A ninth named integer argument under -mgeneral-regs-only requested SIMD
   fillers. Packed stack words now exhaust only their used banks. Later
   anonymous arguments still exhaust their own banks from the updated cursor.

Validation before the full gate:
- Memory crate: 42 PASS, zero failures. Cursor tests cover both layouts,
  adjacent lists, independent positions, partial read/write/copy rejection,
  ended cursors and undersized storage.
- Driver/ABI tests: 47 PASS, zero failures. Darwin integer and packed calls
  cross with Apple clang in both directions at O0/O2. Existing mixed calls
  include named integer stack words before anonymous floating values and
  named floating stack words before anonymous integers. Real FP/vector
  functions remain refused under general-only mode.
- The original runtime, both minimal inputs and the new adjacent-list input
  pass 48 source checks, 16 EvoCC native executions and eight Apple clang
  controls. Both targets, both optimization levels and both interpreters are
  included. All native EvoCC builds use general-only and pac-ret.

Capture: .evidence/darwin-arguments-20261016/, 500 MiB retention cap.
plan.txt and runtime.json keep scope, commands, input/output hashes and exits.
The first RED tests and the second failure that exposed the lifecycle entry
remain. The earlier return-signing captures are unchanged historical inputs.
Acceptance: tools/gate-changed.sh --full-workspace --offline passes 455 Rust
suites: 3,454 PASS, zero failures, eight retained ignores; Clippy and fmt pass.
tools/gate-lean.sh passes all six steps: 62 rule theorems, 36 analysis rows
(576 enumerated instances). The receipt binds EvoIR 2.6.7 and EvoMIR 1.3.5.
These are the shared dirty checkout's gates, not a clean release build.

